  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development, by reason of its inadequate communal kitchen/living space, would represent a substandard and inappropriate form of accommodation which would not be capable of meeting the reasonable needs of occupiers and would be detrimental to the residential amenities of future occupants. The proposal is thereby contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan, Policy CP4 of the Enfield Plan Core Strategy, Policies DMD5 and DMD8 of the Development Management Document, the Mayor of London Housing Supplementary Planning Guidance, The Technical Housing Standards-Nationally Described Space Standards and the guidance contained within the National Planning Policy Framework (2024).",
    "The development, due to insufficient floorspace and inadequate access to outlook and natural daylight, would result in substandard and inappropriate accommodation that fails to meet the reasonable needs of future occupiers. It is therefore considered the development is contrary to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), to Policies D3 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), to Policies CP4 and CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), to Policies DMD5 and DMD8 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), and the Housing Design Standards London Plan Guidance (2023)",
    "The development, by virtue of its inadequate functional floor area due to the low floor-to-ceiling heights, would result in substandard and inappropriate accommodation at Bedroom 6 incapable of meeting the reasonable needs of occupiers contrary to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), to Policies D3 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), to Policies CP4 and CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), to Policies DMD5 and DMD8 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), and the Housing Design Standards London Plan Guidance (2023).",
    "The development, by virtue of the unscreened and oversized 1,100-litre eurobins existing to the front garden, would result in a visually intrusive and incongruous feature that harms the residential character of the street. No suitable screening has been demonstrated, and any enclosure of sufficient size would likely appear overbearing in the residential setting. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies DMD 5 and DMD 8 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), and Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024).",
    "The development, by virtue of its scale and intensity of occupation, would result in unacceptable levels of noise and general disturbance, harming the amenities of neighbouring residential occupiers. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policy DMD 8 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014) and Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024).",
    "The development, in the absence of adequate cycle storage and by virtue of its means of access, location and layout, would fail to provide a secure, convenient and high quality facility for all types of bicycles and would fail to promote or prioritise the use of sustainable modes of transport. The proposal is therefore contrary to Section 9 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies T2, T3, T4, T6, T6.1 and T7 of the London Plan (2021), CP24 and CP25 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD45, DMD46, DMD47 and DMD48 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
